    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="11.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:ICn">I Cn</ref> 11.1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="11.1" corresp="#wit-g-a">And gyf hwa cyricean hæbbe, þe legerstow on ne sig, do he of ða<hi rend="italic">m</hi> nigon dælum his preoste þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> he wylle.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="11.1" corresp="#wit-a">Gif hwa cyricean hæbbe, þe legerstow on ne sy, do he of þam nigon dalum his preoste þæt þæt he wille.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="11.1" corresp="#wit-q">Si quis ęcclesiam habeat, ubi positionis locus non sit, det ex suis nouem partibus presbitero suo quod uelit.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="11.1" corresp="#wit-g-a">And gyf hwa cyricean hæbbe þe legerstow on ne sig, do he of ðam nigon dælum his preoste þæt þæt he wylle.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-g-a">If anyone has a church to which no graveyard is attached, he shall give his priest whatever he desires from the nine [remaining] parts.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">(Und G) Wenn jemand eine [Landguts]kirche hat, an der kein Friedhof ist, entrichte er aus den neun [ihm übrigen] Zehnteln seinem Priester, was er will.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">(And, G) if anyone has an [estate-]church at which there is no graveyard, let him give his priest what he will from the nine [remaining] parts.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">G's ‘And’ is missing from the other MSS and Edgar. Liebermann compares II Eg 2.1.</note>
      </div>
    </body>
